1
00:00:00,125 --> 00:00:00,965
The first thing she did

2
00:00:00,965 --> 00:00:01,949
was to call me

3
00:00:01,949 --> 00:00:04,688
and thank me for the contribution

4
00:00:04,688 --> 00:00:05,639
I had in her life.

5
00:00:05,729 --> 00:00:06,709
Hi, I'm Syaheer.

6
00:00:06,709 --> 00:00:10,069
I've been an MAP Coach since 2011,

7
00:00:10,069 --> 00:00:11,144
which is about 15 years ago.

8
00:00:11,244 --> 00:00:12,923
Hi, I'm Nur Azyyati.

9
00:00:12,923 --> 00:00:15,015
Teaching has always been my passion.

10
00:00:15,125 --> 00:00:16,345
I used to be an educator,

11
00:00:16,345 --> 00:00:19,025
so I've moved out to IT

12
00:00:19,025 --> 00:00:20,152
in corporate roles.

13
00:00:20,152 --> 00:00:22,389
And this is my way of giving back.

14
00:00:22,394 --> 00:00:24,134
I want to help those, especially students

15
00:00:24,134 --> 00:00:26,793
who need more guidance and support.

16
00:00:26,898 --> 00:00:29,158
I get to interact with a lot of students

17
00:00:29,158 --> 00:00:31,398
and I've touched many lives.

18
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:33,208
It's fulfilling to see students

19
00:00:33,208 --> 00:00:35,528
who initially struggle,

20
00:00:35,528 --> 00:00:37,212
doubt themselves or lack motivation

21
00:00:37,212 --> 00:00:38,292
slowly begin to believe

22
00:00:38,292 --> 00:00:39,339
in their own abilities.

23
00:00:39,339 --> 00:00:41,374
Back in 2024, I was teaching

24
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:42,913
a Primary 6 Foundation student.

25
00:00:42,913 --> 00:00:44,199
She has to retake her PSLE.

26
00:00:44,199 --> 00:00:45,119
She told me that

27
00:00:45,119 --> 00:00:46,713
this is the last time.

28
00:00:46,713 --> 00:00:48,508
She worked really, really hard.

29
00:00:48,508 --> 00:00:49,349
She actually passed

30
00:00:49,349 --> 00:00:50,751
her Math Foundation

31
00:00:50,751 --> 00:00:51,787
for the first time.

32
00:00:51,787 --> 00:00:53,307
I hope my students walk away

33
00:00:53,307 --> 00:00:55,327
with greater confidence in themselves

34
00:00:55,327 --> 00:00:56,767
and believe that they are capable

35
00:00:56,767 --> 00:00:58,725
of achieving more than they think.

36
00:00:58,785 --> 00:01:01,115
As the head coaches and coaches

37
00:01:01,115 --> 00:01:02,775
come from many different backgrounds,

38
00:01:02,775 --> 00:01:04,097
not strictly just education.

39
00:01:04,132 --> 00:01:06,172
You don't have to be a perfect educator

40
00:01:06,172 --> 00:01:08,008
because I think every human makes mistakes.

41
00:01:08,008 --> 00:01:10,008
As long as you are passionate,

42
00:01:10,008 --> 00:01:10,648
you have the patience

43
00:01:10,648 --> 00:01:12,668
and you are willing to have

44
00:01:12,668 --> 00:01:14,107
an impact on a child's life.

45
00:01:14,137 --> 00:01:15,772
If you are already thinking about it,

46
00:01:15,772 --> 00:01:16,493
sign up.
